{"reference":"Isaiah 21","book":"Isaiah","chapter":21,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Within Isaiah’s Oracles Against Nations","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"A debated reading of the surrounding material sees Isaiah’s messages addressing Judah, Israel, and foreign nations together: empires may function as instruments, yet they too remain accountable, and the book also looks toward nations learning, worshiping, and sharing in restoration. This larger frame helps place the chapter’s announcements concerning Babylon, Dumah, and Arabia among wider reflections on the fate of nations.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_021_ed1550096bf2e27e2c542e05"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}